15 0 obj
<< /A 38 0 R /Alt (Panel A contains a schematic summarizing study design and workflow for a pediatric cohort including participant groups \(healthy, AR, asthma, CARAS\) with icons, sample sizes, and an overview of quantitative data acquisition and data analysis steps. Panel B presents a scatter plot with colored ellipses illustrating group-wise separation in multivariate analysis. Panel C displays a heatmap of metabolomic features across AR, CARAS, asthma, and healthy control groups, with a color scale indicating relative abundance. Panel D shows three volcano plots comparing differentially expressed features between AR versus healthy, asthma versus healthy, and CARAS versus healthy, highlighting up- and down-regulated points in red, blue, and green.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Panel A displays volcano plots comparing normal versus AR, asthma, and CARAS patients, showing fold change versus corrected p value with significant genes highlighted. Panel B presents OPLS-DA scatter plots with normal group in blue and patient groups \(AR in red, asthma in blue, CARAS in green\) distinctly clustered. Panel C includes model validation plots for each comparison, indicating R squared and Q squared values, with green and blue points representing validation metrics.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a Venn diagram comparing metabolite overlaps among CARAS, AR, and Asthma groups, with percentages and counts indicated for each intersection. Panel B displays a bubble plot of metabolic pathway enrichment where circle size and color represent significance and pathway impact; notable pathways include glyoxylate and dicarboxylate metabolism. Panel C presents a correlation matrix heatmap for metabolite relationships, where colored circles indicate the strength and direction of correlations and asterisks denote significance at p less than or equal to 0.05.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Figure with three panels: panel A shows six violin plots comparing metabolite ratios among Healthy, AR, Asthma, and CARAS groups for LysoPC, Propionic acid, Aminohydroxydodecanoic acid, Eicosadienoic acid, Sarcosine, and Phenylalanine; panel B is a ROC curve with six colored lines, displaying sensitivity and specificity for each metabolite, with LysoPC having the highest AUC of 0.924; panel C is a horizontal bar chart titled \215Metabolites Sets Enrichment Overview,\216 ranking metabolic pathways by enrichment ratio and P value, with Malate-Aspartate Shuttle most enriched.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Metabolic network diagram showing interconnected pathways for glycerophospholipid metabolism, glycine, serine, alanine and threonine metabolism, urea cycle and metabolism, and glycolysis and gluconeogenesis, with key metabolites highlighted in green and blue shapes.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
